<title>HONG KONG: HK Land says 1996 net profit US$649 mln.</title>
<headline>HK Land says 1996 net profit US$649 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)		 24.67    vs 9.78</p>
<p>    Final dividend (U.S. cebts)  8.50     vs 8.00</p>
<p>    Total dividend (U.S. cents)  12.00    vs 11.50</p>
<p>    Net after tax and minority   649.4    vs 256.9</p>
<p>    Net Income from Properties   485.1    vs 465.6</p>
<p>    Company name		     Hongkong Land Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Note - Hongkong Land said net profit increased principally due to a write back of US$217 million arising from the disposal of an interest in Trafalgar House, which generated a US$158 million charge in 1995. Excluding the effect of Trafalgar House in both years, net profit after tax and minority interests grew four percent to US$432 million from US$415 million.</p>
<p>Chairman Simon Keswick said, &quot;Earnings in the current year are expected to be flat as a result of the rental reversion cycle. The progress made on expanding our property and infrastructure interests in the region will, however, provide for longer term growth.&quot;</p>
<p>    Operating profit			 460.7    vs 445.0</p>
<p>    Profit from continuing activities  492.0    vs 469.9</p>
<p>    Discontinued activity		  220.6    vs 145.5 loss</p>
<p>    Profit before taxation		 712.6    vs 324.4</p>
<p>    Retained profit			  333.8    vs 46.1 loss</p>
<p>Share registers closed - April 14-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable -	 June 18.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441</p>
</text>
